  "python_code": "async def act(page):\n    \"\"\"\n    Steps:\n    1. Use the site-aware helper `create_curated_collection_by_search` to perform a visible-site search for the keyword \"Collector\". This helper is required when available because it reliably locates the complementary region search input, triggers the search (with sensible fallbacks), and waits for the main results area to appear. Note: this helper always begins with `await page.goto('/')`, which is acceptable and preferred here to reach the root page where the search widget is present.\n    2. After the helper returns, locate the first search result inside the role=\"main\" region and click its title link. Use accessibility-role-centric chained locators (start from `main`) and call `.count()` before using `.nth()` to avoid indexing errors.\n    3. Make the click the last action because it will navigate away from the current page.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # 1) Perform the visible search via the knowledge-base helper (this navigates to '/' and triggers the search UI)\n    await create_curated_collection_by_search(page, \"Collector\")\n\n    # 2) Locate results inside the main region and click the first article's title link\n    main = page.get_by_role(\"main\")\n    articles = main.get_by_role(\"article\")\n\n    # Ensure we count before indexing to avoid errors\n    count = await articles.count()\n    if count == 0:\n        # No results found; nothing to click.\n        return\n\n    first_article = articles.nth(0)\n    # Use the full chained path to the title link inside the article's heading\n    heading = first_article.get_by_role(\"heading\")\n    title_link = heading.get_by_role(\"link\")\n\n    # Click the first matching title link (final action; expected to navigate)\n    await title_link.first.click()\n",
